1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sun setting
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes go flying too.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,940
Will you take my hand and walk with me,
I wonder?

4
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:39,140
They laugh at me for
still being a kid at heart.

5
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I leave some of my energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
little by little, one yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streets feel strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,240
From the water bottle under the pointed hat,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the sun sinks into the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow, too,
it'll end just like this, won't it?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:20,960
Katsushika, Shibamata, again,
even happiness slips away.

12
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:24,680
Because I'm a fool who only
realized it after hearing it.

13
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:30,760
Delivering unexploded bombs.

14
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:43,100
Traveling through Suruga province,
the scent of tea and...

15
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:45,420
Pretty nice place

16
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:47,360
I found this hidden gem the other day.

17
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:47,820
Yeah,

18
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:52,460
Is it really okay? Skipping work
and coming all the way out here?

19
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:55,220
Even people need a refresh now and then.

20
00:01:55,880 --> 00:02:01,100
Soaking in a hot spring like this is all
for refreshing myself so I can do good work.

21
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,200
Is that so?

22
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:10,260
It's me.

23
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:12,460
Good morning, Ryotsu-kun.

24
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:14,520
And this kid is...

25
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:17,480
I hear you're out on patrol. Good work.

26
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:18,903
No, well,

27
00:02:18,953 --> 00:02:22,960
as an officer stationed at the police box,
it's only natural.

28
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:27,160
Actually, something urgent has come up.
Can you come back right away?

29
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:31,371
Well, I've come all the way to
the far edge of my patrol area,

30
00:02:31,421 --> 00:02:33,020
so I can't really come back right away.

31
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:35,300
You're using Honda-kun's Shiraume, right?

32
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,800
You should be able to come back right away.

33
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:47,040
It broke down, so as soon as it's repaired, we'll come straight back.
Yes, that's right, that's exactly it.

34
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:54,900
Enough, come back right now! Those two went out together,
there's no way they're patrolling properly!

35
00:02:55,390 --> 00:02:57,120
Y-yes

36
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:02,880
What happened, senpai? The Chief found out!
We're heading back to Tokyo right now!

37
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,880
Hurry up!

38
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:09,880
Ah w-wait, w-wait, senpai!

39
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:17,940
Hurry up or we'll leave you behind,
Mr. Ryotsu.

40
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:22,120
Alright, Honda.
But put your clothes on first.

41
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,740
Turn right there.

42
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:28,780
Got it.

43
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:35,240
Hey, you! Don't just jump out like that!

44
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,886
U-um, officer,

45
00:03:37,936 --> 00:03:41,300
we found something huge.
Please come right away.

46
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:44,520
We're in a hurry. Try someone else.

47
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:47,934
While we were plowing the field,
we dug up something amazing.

48
00:03:47,984 --> 00:03:50,080
It's sure to make tomorrow's front page.

49
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,600
Sure to make tomorrow's front page, you say?

50
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:53,840
Wait.

51
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:55,805
Mr. Ryotsu,

52
00:03:55,855 --> 00:04:00,100
isn't this area supposed to be where
the rumors of Tokugawa's buried gold are?

53
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:01,900
Wh-what, buried gold?

54
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:12,120
If things go well, we might get a cut of it.

55
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,300
Hey, show us the way right away.

56
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,520
Over there.

57
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:19,380
Move, move, move, move!

58
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:23,340
Police! Nobody lay a finger on it!

59
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:25,540
Hey, you there, back up, back up!

60
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:28,220
Now then, where's our buried treasure?

61
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:29,660
What do you think, senior?

62
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:30,620
Well...

63
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,700
Th-that's...

64
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:38,900
That's quite an unusual dye box.

65
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:41,120
Is there gold coins inside this?

66
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:45,158
What's this,

67
00:04:45,208 --> 00:04:48,880
What's wrong, everyone?

68
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,522
But senior,

69
00:04:50,572 --> 00:04:54,500
Look at it any way you like, that's a bomb.

70
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:06,340
It's Acacia Park.

71
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,900
That's the spot where the
Tokugawa buried gold is.

72
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:12,580
Nobody said anything about buried gold.

73
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:16,240
That's a wartime dud, right?

74
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,140
Yeah, no doubt about it.

75
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:22,000
At that size, a 50-meter square
would be blown to smithereens.

76
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:24,060
R-really? That much?

77
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,880
Well, the rest is up to you.

78
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:29,620
Officer, wait! Don't be so heartless!

79
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,960
This isn't our jurisdiction.

80
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,380
Then why are you here?

81
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:38,280
Don't tell me the officers
are slacking off...

82
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:41,540
Alright, alright, I'll handle it now.

83
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:51,820
Yes, this is Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box.

84
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:52,360
Is that you, Terai?

85
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:54,280
Is that you?

86
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:58,220
Don't shout! The Chief's still there, right?

87
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:03,620
He's furious already.
You'd better come back right away.

88
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:08,560
We've got a bit of a problem.
We found an unexploded bomb.

89
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:13,240
Wow! Amazing! An unexploded bomb!

90
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:17,825
Amazing? An unexploded bomb?
What are you so excited about?

91
00:06:17,875 --> 00:06:19,280
That Terai guy.

92
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:21,400
That's right! It's an unexploded bomb!

93
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:23,785
It's terrible!

94
00:06:23,835 --> 00:06:27,660
The bomb I bought for
500,000 yen was stolen.

95
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:30,460
Terai, take notes.

96
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:31,500
Right.

97
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:35,420
Well, I bought it for 500,000 yen each...

98
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,900
You bought it for 500,000 yen each?

99
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:39,300
What do you mean?

100
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:42,720
Are you saying you bought an
unexploded bomb for 500,000 yen?

101
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:46,340
While I was having a
soda at a coffee shop...

102
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:47,240
Soda

103
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,620
What do you mean, "soda"? Hey!

104
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:50,640
What's wrong, senpai?

105
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:54,480
Terai says he's going to buy an
unexploded bomb for 500,000 yen.

106
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,680
What? No way.

107
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,300
No, he really said that.

108
00:06:58,300 --> 00:06:59,740
Ask him yourself.

109
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:04,540
Hello, Terai-san,
are you really going to buy a bomb?

110
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:08,780
I've got a sweet tooth in the mornings,
I love cake especially.

111
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,120
Loves cake?

112
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,780
He says he loves weapons.

113
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:15,320
No doubt about it.

114
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:20,560
He didn't look like the type who'd
be into that sort of thing, though.

115
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,760
Wait a minute...

116
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:26,760
Glasses, a chubby build,
a wishy-washy personality...

117
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:29,200
He's the very picture of a geek!

118
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:34,460
And on top of that, he bought a house way out in the middle of nowhere.
Suspicious!

119
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,580
Could it be that...

120
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:41,080
he's hiding his dangerous
hobby from the world?

121
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,280
Bombs are great, aren't they?

122
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:46,620
I've got it! Terai's true identity!

123
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,520
He's a hardcore military otaku!

124
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:52,040
And on top of that! He's a bomb maniac!

125
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:56,200
Alright, Utter!
Get the cash ready and wait for me!

126
00:07:58,840 --> 00:07:59,880
Oh no, that's bad.

127
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:02,120
Hello? Ryo-san?

128
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,220
The line went dead.

129
00:08:04,780 --> 00:08:06,560
What on earth did he want?

130
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,380
When I contacted the main station,

131
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:14,200
they said there could still be
unexploded bombs buried around here.

132
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:18,880
So I need you two to help search for them.

133
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:22,340
Shouldn't the police be
handling something like that?

134
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:24,360
This is your turf, after all.

135
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:29,060
Removing dangerous objects yourselves
is only right as decent people.

136
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:31,600
Yeah, this is dangerous, isn't it?

137
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:33,340
Dangerous, dangerous!

138
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,880
Stop trying to take on
the dud bomb for real!

139
00:08:37,940 --> 00:08:40,140
You care more about
money than unexploded bombs

140
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:48,640
How about you? Did you find anything?

141
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:49,300
No luck.

142
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:50,320
Nothing.

143
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:54,920
After all that searching, we only found two.

144
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:58,800
Two for a million yen, not bad at all.

145
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:01,900
Alright, Honda! Carry this one!

146
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,740
Us?

147
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:07,840
Of course! It's our duty as police officers!

148
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:12,840
Have you forgotten?
Terai is buying this one for 500,000 yen!

149
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:14,580
B-but...

150
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:15,100
Officer!

151
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:18,320
It's the real thing, but will this do?

152
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:21,400
Perfect! Tie it up in front of the castle!

153
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:26,160
Loading's done! Let's go!

154
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:29,420
Let's just call this off after all...
It's dangerous...

155
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:31,680
Get in the Hakubai!

156
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:35,040
Once you grab the wheel, that timid
little bug of yours will blow away, right?

157
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:44,420
What's wrong?

158
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:48,340
I'm too anxious to feel brave at all.

159
00:09:48,340 --> 00:09:49,580
Don't worry.

160
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:53,060
It hasn't gone off in over
fifty years since the war.

161
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:55,240
It's not going to explode now.

162
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:59,120
And if we're going to die, it's my fate too.

163
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:01,660
Senpai

164
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:15,220
Looks like we're okay after all.

165
00:10:15,220 --> 00:10:18,020
Senpai, you said we'd die together,
didn't you?

166
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:21,940
Sorry, sorry. My body just moved on reflex.

167
00:10:21,940 --> 00:10:25,820
There we go.
Now we know it won't explode easily.

168
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:30,280
Now all you have to do is drive
carefully so you don't jolt it.

169
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:32,880
Yeah, yeah, got it.

170
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:37,060
After all, I'm destined to follow
you to the depths of hell anyway.

171
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:38,980
Well, you understand well.

172
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:48,840
This guy may have taken the wrong road.

173
00:10:49,860 --> 00:10:52,760
Even though I drove
exactly as you instructed.

174
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:58,580
Shut up! You're the one who said you hated driving on the highway,
so I went and found back roads for you!

175
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:03,760
But with two of us on a rickshaw cart,
pulling a bomb, we can't get on the highway!

176
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:05,680
We'll get stopped at the toll booth.

177
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:08,920
Just sound the siren and push right
through so nobody can say a word.

178
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:11,700
You do this all the time, you know that?

179
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:14,680
That's totally reckless!

180
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:19,520
The steering suddenly got lighter.
Did the road get better?

181
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:22,240
Doesn't feel like it, though.

182
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:25,140
The cart's come off!

183
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:26,440
Not getting away!

184
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,800
Two of them for a million yen.

185
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:31,640
Got 'em! We caught up!

186
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:36,000
If we crash, it's all over!

187
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:48,840
Senpai, are you all right?

188
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:53,700
Yeah, yeah, somehow.

189
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:09,140
Senpai, are you really
planning to carry it like this?

190
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:12,020
The cart's gone,
so there's no other choice, okay?

191
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:15,220
But if it tips over, it'll explode!

192
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:16,460
Then just don't let it tip over.

193
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:21,460
What? Seriously, where are we?

194
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:22,660
Senpai!

195
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:27,000
Senpai! Help me!

196
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:29,220
What's with that bird?!

197
00:12:29,380 --> 00:12:30,700
Please hurry and help me!

198
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,560
Is this really Japan?

199
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:34,780
Kanan!

200
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:36,400
Kanan!

201
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:42,080
Please stop! It's going to explode!

202
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:43,760
I see.

203
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,660
Senpai!

204
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:47,560
Honda!

205
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,360
Wait!

206
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:54,080
We have to run! If we drop it like this,
we're in big trouble!

207
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:56,280
Hey! Honda! Don't let go of the bomb!

208
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:57,820
It's 500,000 yen apiece!

209
00:12:58,180 --> 00:13:01,000
I'm not joking! My life matters more!

210
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:04,620
When the money comes in, you get 10%!
No, make that 20%!

211
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:06,880
It's tied so tightly!

212
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:08,160
Wean-kun!

213
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,900
Whoa! Eyes again!

214
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,180
Is this some kind of monster movie?

215
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:22,520
500,000 yen!

216
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:28,320
Dad, Mom, Grandpa, Grandma, it's huge!

217
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:32,140
And then, come here, Nana-chan,
forgive me for this untimely death!

218
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:34,300
500,000 yen!

219
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:41,640
We're not safe yet! Wait!

220
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:45,840
Uh-oh!

221
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:52,820
We made it in time.

222
00:13:56,820 --> 00:13:58,840
Hey, don't thrash around!

223
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:01,660
Hurry up and do something, senpai!

224
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:02,760
Just hang on, now!

225
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:07,780
Clank-clatter!

226
00:14:09,380 --> 00:14:10,680
It's a tunnel!

227
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:14,100
Uh-oh, it's going to be a tight fit!

228
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,220
Tetetetete

229
00:14:23,220 --> 00:14:25,760
Good thing we've got this beat-up truck.

230
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,160
Seriously.

231
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:29,800
I've lost about a hundred years off my life.

232
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:30,240
Perfect.

233
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,320
Let's have it carried all
the way into town like this.

234
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:35,640
But if we go wandering around
town carrying this thing,

235
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:37,120
it'll cause a huge uproar!

236
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:39,260
Yeah, you've got a point.

237
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:41,440
Think of something good...

238
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:41,760
Ah

239
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,080
Here it is.

240
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,000
Look, a giant kokeshi doll.

241
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,160
Nobody will suspect a thing with this.

242
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:52,300
You think so?

243
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,200
For crying out loud.

244
00:14:56,960 --> 00:15:00,660
We have to wait over an
hour for the next train.

245
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:03,540
Never underestimate a rural local line.

246
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:05,440
Let's rest somewhere.

247
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:06,540
Yeah.

248
00:15:09,340 --> 00:15:13,120
Unbelievable,
not even one café in front of the station.

249
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,800
There's nothing we can do.

250
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:31,780
Isn't this one the same too, peccha?

251
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:34,540
Yeah, I'll take it along
while I'm at it, peccha.

252
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:36,660
This is pretty heavy, peccha.

253
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:38,620
Because there's all sorts
of stuff in it, peccha.

254
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:45,820
Damn, I dozed off without meaning to.

255
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:49,440
Wah... it's gone!

256
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:49,640
Gone!

257
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:53,140
What's wrong, senpai?

258
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:55,420
Gone! Gone! Gone! Gone!

259
00:15:56,220 --> 00:15:58,400
What's gone, senpai?

260
00:15:58,580 --> 00:16:00,260
The unexploded bomb has vanished!

261
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,680
Eeeeeeeh?!

262
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:02,800
Damn it, where is it?!

263
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:04,440
Two of them add up to a million yen!

264
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:05,880
You bastard!

265
00:16:06,820 --> 00:16:08,660
Do you know where the unexploded
bomb that was right here went?

266
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,640
Th-the unexploded bomb, you say?

267
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,940
Senpai,
right now it looks like a kokeshi doll.

268
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:14,800
Right.

269
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:17,620
Hey, don't you know about
the kokeshi that was here?

270
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:23,120
I-if it's a kokeshi,
it's over at that kokeshi temple, I bet.

271
00:16:23,380 --> 00:16:24,460
The kokeshi temple, you idiot.

272
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:28,860
Today's the kokeshi memorial day, so there
should be a whole bunch of them gathered there.

273
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:33,380
Senpai, wait up!

274
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:34,380
Go, go, go!

275
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:41,570
Please, hey, hey, hold on a second,

276
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:44,520
What are you on about hmm,
what the hell do you mean?

277
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,000
What's this?

278
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:54,720
Blah blah blah, blah blah blah, blah blah.

279
00:16:54,720 --> 00:17:02,000
Blah blah blah, blah blah blah, blah blah.

280
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:06,600
W-what is this, kokeshi... what on earth?

281
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,860
Don't tell me it's already been burned up!

282
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:12,420
You don't think an unexploded bomb
thrown into a fire would be fine, do you?

283
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:14,840
Search! It must still be somewhere!

284
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:17,000
Easier said than done.

285
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,300
-What's going on?-Ow! Stop it!

286
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:24,160
One million yen!

287
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:27,920
Senpai!

288
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:31,980
Hot! Hot! Hot!

289
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:35,440
Water! Water! Water! It's hot!

290
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:38,440
Senpai! Are you all right?

291
00:17:39,020 --> 00:17:40,620
Somehow, yeah.

292
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,560
Now that we've come this far, we can relax.

293
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:49,700
All that's left is changing trains.

294
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,680
But this outfit is so embarrassing.

295
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:54,940
Just put up with it.

296
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:58,520
This outfit is the best
way to avoid suspicion.

297
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,680
Poor thing

298
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:02,240
How pitiful

299
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:04,420
His wife must have run off on him

300
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:06,280
Look at that face.

301
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:07,940
Doesn't look like there's
any way out for him, either.

302
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:10,140
It's black magic, what kind of magic?

303
00:18:10,140 --> 00:18:12,960
Shut up! I'm still single!

304
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:15,880
So I'm an unmarried father after all.

305
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,280
Well, how remarkable

306
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:19,620
I hear that kind of thing
is popular in the city.

307
00:18:19,620 --> 00:18:22,800
Drill, what does a baby's face look like

308
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:24,440
Stop it, don't look!

309
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:26,820
Hey, isn't the top part nice?

310
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:29,980
Hey, don't touch!

311
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,520
Please, have mercy!

312
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:39,780
Surely you can grant a little wish from
an old man with so little time left.

313
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:43,200
Are you sure you want that little
time left to get even shorter?

314
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:45,540
Next stop: Otai-daimae.

315
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:47,680
Otai-daimae.

316
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:52,540
What's going on?

317
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:53,340
Yeah.

318
00:18:57,700 --> 00:18:58,900
But this one's male.

319
00:18:58,900 --> 00:18:59,740
It's not male.

320
00:19:04,180 --> 00:19:06,100
Honda, are you all right?

321
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,620
Not at all, I'm not all right.

322
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:12,860
Senpai.

323
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,720
Help!

324
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,900
What's wrong, Honda?

325
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:29,100
The bomb's gone!

326
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:31,160
What?!

327
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:32,620
The bomb?

328
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:33,780
No way!

329
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:34,640
You're joking, right?

330
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:36,460
W-what is this?!

331
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:38,600
Aaaaaah!

332
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:42,080
Move, move, this guy's going to -

333
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:46,900
That's it, keep coming this way!

334
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:54,240
Get out of the way! Move already,
can't you see we're coming through!

335
00:19:56,580 --> 00:19:58,040
Don't get in our way this time!

336
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:00,520
Hey! You lot!

337
00:20:10,840 --> 00:20:12,320
Whoa! Watch out!

338
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:15,260
Healthy as ever!

339
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,340
Sure enough.

340
00:20:26,260 --> 00:20:28,040
My balloon...

341
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:31,000
Sorry, kid. Did we scare you?

342
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,900
Aren't you dangerous,
doing that in a place like this?

343
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:36,620
Good thing it was a clumsy guy like him.

344
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:42,400
We finally made it.

345
00:20:43,620 --> 00:20:47,400
Pull yourself together, Honda.
The goal's just a little further.

346
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:49,320
Just a little further, you say?

347
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:53,000
Chief

348
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:57,240
A pair of men dressed like police officers
Translation>
caused a bomb scare on the train,

349
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:59,880
so I came to check, and

350
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:02,380
it's you two after all.

351
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:04,420
Please calm down, Chief!

352
00:21:04,420 --> 00:21:05,820
This calls for my sword!

353
00:21:05,820 --> 00:21:07,060
No more talk!

354
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:08,520
That rotten disposition of yours

355
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:11,000
I'll knock straight into you from the root!

356
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,780
That's dangerous, isn't it!

357
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:16,780
You know how skilled I am at kendo.

358
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:19,420
Yes, I won't cause any
trouble for the citizens!

359
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:22,020
But it's still dangerous, I'm telling you!

360
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:24,740
Stop spouting your nonsensical gibberish!

361
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:28,320
It won't fall! Wait!

362
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:32,420
Where's the ticket? Where's the ticket?

363
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:38,240
If it's come to this, I have to hand this
over to Terai right away and get the million!

364
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:39,840
Yes!

365
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:42,460
I'm back!

366
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,180
R-Ryo-chan!

367
00:21:44,180 --> 00:21:45,600
I brought it, Terai!

368
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,220
Two for a million.

369
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:48,680
Now hurry up and pay.

370
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,980
What are you talking about, Ryo-san?

371
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:53,020
The unexploded bomb, the unexploded bomb!

372
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:55,860
You said you'd buy it for 500,000 each,

373
00:21:55,860 --> 00:21:58,520
so we carried it all the way here with such hardship,
didn't we?

374
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:01,460
Is, is that the real thing?

375
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:02,800
Of course it is.

376
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:04,540
Now hurry up and hand over the money.

377
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:07,220
I-I never said that!

378
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:07,900
Don't be so stingy.

379
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:09,240
When I made the phone call,

380
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:11,780
you said you bought the unexploded bomb for 500,000 yen apiece,
didn't you?

381
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:14,220
When Ryo-san called,

382
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:17,680
a strong gust of wind blew in that time,

383
00:22:18,460 --> 00:22:20,560
Whoa, what a powerful blast of wind!

384
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,840
What a powerful blast of wind!

385
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:26,260
When that old man whose
urn was stolen came in,

386
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:28,800
the culprit was found right away, though.

387
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:32,680
Right, right,
I took down the old man's story in my notes,

388
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:35,120
bought one for 500,000 yen.

389
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:37,520
What a powerful blast of wind!

390
00:22:38,360 --> 00:22:40,200
bought one for 500,000 yen.

391
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:46,400
So you misheard that as him saying he bought
an unexploded bomb for 500,000 yen apiece

392
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:50,660
Good grief!

393
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:56,800
Oh my, waiting properly at the police box?
That's a good attitude.

394
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,220
Chief, well, you see...

395
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:00,520
Prepare yourself!

396
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:07,940
Stop! What if you hit the
unexploded bomb on my back?

397
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:12,560
Unexploded, you say? Do you really
think an excuse like that will work?!

398
00:23:13,300 --> 00:23:14,420
You...

399
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:17,640
Pistol!

400
00:23:20,060 --> 00:23:22,100
Shinken Shiraha-dori!

401
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:23,600
Phew, I'm saved...

402
00:23:24,340 --> 00:23:25,620
Two-sword style!

403
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:42,680
Why didn't you tell me
it was the real thing?

404
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:46,360
I did tell you, Chief.
You just didn't believe me!

405
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:49,180
This happens because of your
bad behavior day in and day out!

406
00:23:49,180 --> 00:23:51,820
You brought this on yourself
by not trusting Fuga!

407
00:23:51,820 --> 00:23:54,280
How could I trust anything you say?

408
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:59,060
I never want to go out
with you senpai again!

409
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:06,520
See?

410
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:09,600
No matter how many monks
come with the police box,

411
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:12,280
if I die, this show is over, you know!

412
00:24:12,280 --> 00:24:14,020
Do you understand that?

413
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:16,580
Hey, whoever's in charge, come out!

414
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:18,300
Next time

415
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:19,380
Ryotsu Dies

416
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:21,700
What? This isn't good!

417
00:24:39,220 --> 00:24:43,720
With spirit,
solve it quickly and thoroughly.

418
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:54,200
Decided, inspired, bouncing,
gathered, into action.

419
00:24:54,200 --> 00:25:00,400
Flying off, power above all for sumo.

420
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:12,720
Everyone gather here,
the dreamlike final energy.

421
00:25:13,760 --> 00:25:23,840
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, painting the universe,
standing on the ground, Kameari's star spun around in a circle.

422
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:28,960
"This'll do, right?" "As if it would!"

423
00:25:37,580 --> 00:25:40,560
Thanks for watching.

